   "error": null,
   "response_text": "Fixed it. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**Cause:** In `invkit/pricing.py`, `bulk_discount()` used a strict-greater comparison:\n\n```python\nif quantity > BULK_THRESHOLD:   # BULK_THRESHOLD = 10\n```\n\nThat fires the 5% discount only at 11+, excluding the \"10 or more\" boundary the policy actually specifies (classic off-by-one \u2014 the spec literally says \"10 or more\", so `>` was just wrong; `>=` is the correct operator here).\n\n**Fix:** Changed to `if quantity >= BULK_THRESHOLD:`. One-line change, library source only, no tests touched.\n\n**Verification:** existing suite passes (4 passed), and boundary check confirms 9 \u2192 0.0, 10 \u2192 5.0, 11 \u2192 5.5.\n\nDONE",
